{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1379717-general-hunter-groups-fan-made-homebrew-ideas-speculation","id":1379717,"title":"General Hunter Groups, fan-made/homebrew ideas & speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-09T03:09:04-07:00","id":1379717,"title":"General Hunter Groups, fan-made/homebrew ideas & speculation","content":"I'm pretty confident that a thread on this subject has been done before. I found at least one a while ago. However, I have never been able to find it since, which is really disappointing because I remember it had some great ideas on it. No recollection as to what those ideas were, but they were great ones. So I'm going to start a new thread on the topic. If that old thread gets found, please merge this one with that.<br /> Just gonna establish what the different kinds of groups there are in Hunter culture.<br /> <br /> Cells: Hunter tier 1.<br /> Compacts: Hunter tier 2.<br /> Conspiracies: Hunter tier 3.<br /> Confederacies: Hunter tier 4.<br /> Conventions: not entirely sure what these are but they appear to be an odd mix between the Compacts of tier 2 &amp; the Conspiracies of tier 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 04-09-2020, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:13:47-07:00","id":1379719,"title":"","content":"A Japanese compact/conspiracy born out of the JSDF. Might be in the process of schisming on the subject of how to interact with Radiant Nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:48:38-07:00","id":1379883,"title":"","content":"The Abyssal Guard<br /> Compact based around combating the Abyss. Have some method to identify Abyssal stuff.<br /> Unknown how much information about the Abyss they have &amp; how accurate it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:51:37-07:00","id":1379885,"title":"","content":"House of Candles<br /> Born in a small town in Mexico. Believe in God the Nomadic Divinity as opposed to God the Creator. Wield an Endowment called the Light (?) which is primarily a spiritual tool. Arguably Christian.<br /> Divided into three factions: the Healers; the Investigators; &amp; the Soldiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:02:44-07:00","id":1379887,"title":"","content":"Inspired Conspiracy<br /> The name comes from the fact that they oppose the Inspired, the protagonists of the fan-made gameline Genius: The Transgression.<br /> The reason for the opposition is because the Inspired are not real scientist, &amp; thus their existence is inherently offensive (at least to the Conspiracy).<br /> <br /> Origin: Age of Enlightenment<br /> Joining: possible/potential members must show sufficient understanding of an Academic subject.<br /> <br /> Endowment: Techne<br /> As they are opposed to the Inspired, their Endowment is built to work in that conflict &amp; has two functions.<br /> One, it provides resistance to becoming a Beholden or Inspired.<br /> Two, it can affect Wonders, causing their potential to fall to Havoc to increase, decrease, or control how it falls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:06:02-07:00","id":1379890,"title":"","content":"Krato, if you're going to start a thread, isnt it best you edit your first post rather than just making new posts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:11:15-07:00","id":1379892,"title":"","content":"The Wielders of the Manifested Keys<br /> Cannot become possessed by a Geist &amp; become one of the Bound, but can use the Manifestations &amp; Keys that the Bound do.<br /> Each combination of Manifestation &amp; Key must be bought separately &amp; acts as a 1-5 dot power depending on how it's treated in Geist: The Sin-Eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T23:12:19-07:00","id":1380034,"title":"","content":"So about that other thread covering Hunter Compacts &amp; Conspiracies, I remembered one of the groups.<br /> Taking into account that it was a long time ago (&amp; thus might be rife with misremembering stuff) &amp; building on that a bit, here's what I have on the group:<br /> <br /> The Sect of the Returning Light<br /> This is a compact or conspiracy of demon-blooded.<br /> They are a splinter faction of the Lucifuge, most likely deriving from the philosophical faction, Reconciliation. They take the core concept behind this philosophy (that the Devil is bound to evil because of how much darkness is in the world, &amp; that must free him) &amp; apply it to the entirety of demonkind (that's ephemeral demons, they're not sure what the other ones are). <br /> Their Endowment allows them to summon forth minor Inferno demons to serve them.<br /> The Lady of Milan has declared them to be heretical.<br /> They have less power &amp; coordination than the Lucifuge. Whereas the Lucifuge has merely 666 members, the Sect of the Returning Light has potentially thousands, however they are in many little factions each of which has less members than the Lucifuge as a whole.<br /> <br /> There is another group from the mystery thread that I remember, but that has been posted on multiple, findable places so I don't feel the need to rehash what I know of that one.<br /> For those who want to go looking for it, it is a magical girl conspiracy (unconnected to Princess: The Hopeful) that draws its power from Arcadia/the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 04-11-2020, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T14:27:54-07:00","id":1380205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1379717-general-hunter-groups-fan-made-homebrew-ideas-speculation?p=1379890#post1379890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Krato, if you're going to start a thread, isnt it best you edit your first post rather than just making new posts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but this strategy/layout/etc. feels comfortable to me &amp; that seems more important than what is easy or best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T17:11:47-07:00","id":1380241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div clas